{"id":"9545c1a9-c3ca-46fa-ad92-280a8f93b4f4","object":"chat.completion","created":1793242508,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"thought\": \"I have the stats_logger key mechanisms (log worker, emit, logger init). Now write a note for stats_logger, then continue reading the remaining files.\", \"code\": \"write_note(title='stats_logger mechanisms', content='stats_logger.py imports logging via `from deepinfer.logger import init_logger` and creates module logger at line 29: `logger = init_logger(__name__)`. The real queue consumer is `_log_worker(q)`: iterates `for msgs in iter(q.get, None)`, sleeps based on `dist.get_rank() % 8`, then `for m in msgs: logger.info(m)` and sets need_sleep = q.empty(); exceptions go to traceback.print_exc(). Producer `_emit_logs` puts msgs list on queue. The only place to add `extra={\\\"keep_full_message\\\": True}` is the `logger.info(m)` call inside _log_worker, preserving queue, ordering, sleep, sentinel and exception handling.', evidence_ids=['ev-ddb5be78a5cf6218d616','ev-c8859274b7c70879ff16','ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813','ev-5abfdabfb975754c6683'], section='')\"}"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":7091,"completion_tokens":283,"total_tokens":7374,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5376},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":5376,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1715},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}